{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And a fire went out.</b> At first it is stated without specification, and afterward Scripture explained how it went out: ״ויקחו בני אהרן נדב ואביהוא״ etc. <b>And a fire went out from before HaShem and consumed them</b> — this is the going out of the fire mentioned above. For the way it went out: from before HaShem, from the Holy of Holies, it found Nadav and Avihu in front of the golden altar that is in the Hekhal, offering strange fire upon it, and it consumed them. And that fire went out from the Hekhal to the outside, onto the altar of burnt offering, and consumed upon it the burnt offering etc." "<b>And a fire went out.</b> Rashi: Rabbi Eliezer says — the sons of Aharon died only because they ruled a halakhah in the presence of Moshe their master. That is, they reasoned: even though the fire descends from heaven, there is a commandment to bring it from an ordinary source, as it says ״ונתנו בני אהרן אש״ etc. And they did not ask Moshe their master, as it is written ״אשר לא צוה אותם״ — and it was incumbent upon them to consult Moshe their master, as we learned in tractate Ta'anit: Yoshiyahu was punished and killed because he should have consulted Yirmeyahu and did not consult him, when Pharaoh Necho passed through his land with sword. And one may say: they erred in the ruling to offer strange fire on that very day. And what is written ״ונתנו בני אהרן הכהנים אש״ — even though the fire descends from heaven, there is a commandment to bring it from an ordinary source — that applies from that day onward, when it had already descended from heaven; but on that day, when it had not yet descended from heaven, and the Holy One, blessed be He, wished to be glorified through it before all the people, He did not command them. And that is what is written ״אשר לא צוה אותם״ — so as not to diminish the honor of the Shekhinah, as we find with Eliyahu: ״ואש לא תשימו.״" "<b>And consumed them and they died.</b> Measure for measure — they were punished here with fire, for we find in the appearance of the glory of the Shekhinah that it is like consuming fire, and they were warned concerning it at Sinai, as Rashi explained in parashat Mishpatim regarding ״ויחזו את האלהים,״ and concerning the elders of Israel ״באש תבערה״ in parashat Beha'alotekha. Another interpretation: measure for measure — they sinned here with fire and were stricken with fire." "<b>And they died before HaShem.</b> Rabbi Eliezer says: they died only in the outside, a place where the Levites are permitted to enter, as it says ״ויקרבו כל העדה וישאום בכתנותם.״ If so, why is it stated ״וימתו לפני ה׳״? The angel struck them and pushed them outside and brought them out. Rabbi Akiva says: they died only in the inside, as it says <b>וימתו לפני ה'</b>. If so, why is it stated ״ויקרבו וישאום בכתנותם״? This teaches that they cast an iron spear and dragged them and brought them out to the outside."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:04.295760876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}